{{#> main title="Home" }}
  <h1>Machine Learning Analysis of Counter-Strike 2 Professional Matches</h1>
  
  <div class="hero-section">
    <p class="lead">A comprehensive exploration of machine learning techniques applied to competitive esports data, achieving <strong>86.65% accuracy</strong> in predicting round outcomes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Project Overview</h2>
    <p>This project applies supervised and unsupervised machine learning methods to professional Counter-Strike 2 match data. By parsing game demos and engineering state-based features, multiple algorithms were trained to predict round winners and discover patterns in player behavior.</p>
    
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <h3>86.65%</h3>
        <p>Best Model Accuracy</p>
        <span>(Gradient Boosting)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <h3>0.942</h3>
        <p>ROC AUC Score</p>
        <span>(Excellent Discrimination)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <h3>2,507</h3>
        <p>Training Samples</p>
        <span>(13 Professional Matches)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <h3>22</h3>
        <p>Engineered Features</p>
        <span>(State-Based)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Key Finding: Economy Dominates</h2>
    <p>The most significant discovery is that <strong>equipment advantage</strong> is the #1 predictor of round outcomes, accounting for 28.2% of feature importance. Teams with superior weapon loadouts have dramatically higher win probabilities, quantitatively confirming what experienced players understand intuitively.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Methods Explored</h2>
    <div class="methods-grid">
      <div class="method-card supervised">
        <h4>Supervised Learning</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Gradient Boosting (86.65%)</li>
          <li>AdaBoost (83.33%)</li>
          <li>XGBoost (83.33%)</li>
          <li>Decision Trees</li>
          <li>Naive Bayes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="method-card unsupervised">
        <h4>Unsupervised Learning</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>K-Means Clustering</li>
          <li>Hierarchical Clustering</li>
          <li>PCA Dimensionality Reduction</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Navigation</h2>
    <p>Use the navigation menu above to explore each section of this analysis:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Introduction:</strong> Project background and research questions</li>
      <li><strong>DataPrep & EDA:</strong> Data collection, cleaning, and exploratory analysis</li>
      <li><strong>Clustering:</strong> K-Means and Hierarchical clustering for player role discovery</li>
      <li><strong>PCA:</strong> Principal Component Analysis for dimensionality reduction</li>
      <li><strong>Naive Bayes:</strong> Multinomial and Bernoulli Naive Bayes classification</li>
      <li><strong>Decision Trees:</strong> Tree-based classification with Gini and Entropy criteria</li>
      <li><strong>Boosting:</strong> AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost ensemble methods</li>
      <li><strong>Results:</strong> Comprehensive comparison of all methods</li>
      <li><strong>Project Challenges:</strong> Technical obstacles and lessons learned</li>
      <li><strong>Conclusions:</strong> Key findings and future directions</li>
    </ul>
